y refers to the art and science of food preparation and consumption, which is important in creating palatable diets for dysphagia patients.", "DYSPHAGIA DIET FOOD TEXTURE DESCRIPTORS:", "UNIDAD DE NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA Y DIETÉTICA:The \"UNIDAD DE NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA Y DIETÉTICA\" (Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit) at HUPA is dedicated to providing dietary management and nutritional support for patients, with a particular emphasis on those experiencing swallowing disorders. This unit works closely with the hospital kitchen to ensure that patients receive appropriate dietary care tailored to their specific needs.", "SERVICIO DE COCINA:The \"SERVICIO DE COCINA\" is the kitchen service within hospitals that plays a crucial role in the nutritional care of patients. It is responsible for preparing and serving meals that meet the specific dietary needs of patients, including those with dysphagia. The Servicio de Cocina collaborates closely with the dysphagia unit to develop modified texture menus tailored to the requirements of these patients. Overall, the kitchen service ensures that all meals provided to patients are not only nutritious but also aligned with their individual dietary restrictions and health needs.", "CALIDAD:CALIDAD refers to the quality of nutrients, emphasizing that not all food sources offer the same benefits for growth and health. It encompasses the overall attributes of clinical nutrition products, which include sensory, physical-chemical, and nutritional aspects that must be maintained to ensure efficacy. Additionally, CALIDAD pertains to the standards and certifications that guarantee products meet specified requirements, ensuring their reliability and safety. Furthermore, it includes the standards of food preparation and service in hospitals, which are essential for patient satisfaction and health. Overall, CALIDAD represents a comprehensive approach to ensuring high-quality nutrition and food services across various contexts.", "DRE:DRE, or disease-related malnutrition, is a condition that can significantly impact patients' health and is influenced by the quality of food provided in hospitals. In particular, DRE is identified and evaluated in patients with Alzheimer’s disease to tailor their nutritional treatment effectively. This highlights the importance of addressing nutritional needs in the management of various health conditions, ensuring that patients receive appropriate dietary support to improve their overall well-being.", "CALIDAD DE LOS ALIMENTOS:Food quality in hospitals is evaluated based on patient satisfaction and nutritional standards.", "SISTEMAS DE PRODUCCIÓN:Various systems for food production in hospitals, including traditional and modern cooking methods.", "LÍNEA CALIENTE:A traditional food service system in hospitals that maintains food at high temperatures until consumption.", "LÍNEA FRÍA REFRIGERADA:A food service system that uses refrigeration to preserve food quality in hospitals.", "LÍNEA FRÍA CONGELADA:A food service system that involves freezing food for hospital patients.", "LÍNEA AL VACÍO:A modern cooking method used in hospital food service that preserves food quality.", "CALIDAD ORGANOLÉPTICA:CALIDAD ORGANOLÉPTICA refers to the sensory quality attributes of food, which encompass taste, smell, appearance, and texture. These attributes are crucial for patient meals, as they significantly influence patient satisfaction in hospitals. Ensuring high calidad organoléptica in food served to patients is essential for enhancing their overall dining experience and well-being.", "ALIMENTACIÓN HOSPITALARIA:Alimentación Hospitalaria is a publication that focuses on dietary practices within hospital settings. It aims to provide insights and information related to the nutritional aspects of patient care in healthcare facilities."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1